ou know it takes a hit on your  scholarship if you're serving on yet  that extra committee and so the question  of so the only other piece of advice  that i would give  is after recognizing that it isn't going  to change  is also know that though you step  forward and you step back and we work  and and we  we you have to work as a team so that's  why you do have to work in community i  was just emailing one of my colleagues  about  some you know issue around you know  diversity and  and and my colleague was like you know  i'm tired i am so tired  i'm glad  and you know we're like  we're grown right we're like in our 40s  we're like i'm tired and i emailed my  colleague back  um  and said  yeah i get it i'm i'm i'm on this now  and you take a break because that's what  we do we you know we take turns and you  rest up and then you'll get back in it  and my colleague will  uh and so that's the other thing we have  to be there for each other and be  willing to and be willing  my colleague needed to take the break at  that moment so you've got to also know  that you when you when that time comes  for you and you need to step back you  need to finish your paper you need to  study for that exam  give yourself that liberty  to step back do what you need to do  because  the fight will be there and it needs you  rested and ready  so  i have to apologize to all of you who  sent in some tremendously thoughtful  questions um in the interest of your  time and in your time i'm going to ask  you guys one more question  so the last question uh what's one short  thing you'd like to leave with the  audience professor foreman if you'd like  to go first  give one thing to leave them what would  it be  i would say love  and i say that  because i feel like like love is not a  concept that we talk enough about in law  school  and i don't think it's something we talk  enough about in even in the university  setting  when i when i started this alternative  school for kids in the juvenile jus